.Dd July 24, 2026
.Dt FRAMEWORK_AUTOROTATE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm framework_autorotate
.Nd Framework Laptop 12 X11 display autorotate
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl hv
.Op Fl i Ar msec
.Op Fl m Ar always|tablet
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
orients the built-in display of a Framework Laptop 12 under
.Fx
X11 by reading the Chrome Embedded Controller
.Pq EC
memmap accelerometer and tablet-mode bit
.Pq TBMD ,
then applying
.Xr xrandr 1
to the internal panel
.Pq eDP/LVDS/DSI
and remapping absolute touch and stylus devices to that panel.
Extended external heads are left alone.
.Pp
The service is intended for use with an X display manager greeter as well
as an interactive session.
On logout it can recover greeter orientation with a double-flip and
recenter the XDM
.Nm xlogin
window onto the built-in panel via
.Pa xlogin_recenter .
.Pp
.Sy Framework Laptop 13 Pro
.Pq even with the touchscreen display kit
is
.Em out of scope :
it is a clamshell, not a convertible
.Pq no 360 hinge / tablet mode .
Touchscreen alone is not a reason to port this daemon; that kit also uses a
different touch HID.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-m always|tablet"
.It Fl h
Print a usage summary and exit.
.It Fl v
Verbose.
Can be specified multiple times (up to 2).
.It Fl i Ar msec
Poll interval in milliseconds (minimum 50; default 500).
.It Fl m Ar always|tablet
Rotation mode.
.Cm always
(the default) rotates whenever the accelerometer reports a stable
orientation.
.Cm tablet
rotates only while the EC tablet-mode bit is set; otherwise the panel
is forced to
.Cm normal .
.El
.Sh OPERATION
.Nm
opens
.Pa /dev/io
for EC LPC and memmap access; no kernel module is required at runtime.
.Pp
After each successful RandR:
.Bl -enum
.It
Runs the touch remap helper
.Pa map-touchscreen
with
.Fl W
.Pq no stylus watcher
to keep ILIT absolute pointers aligned with the built-in panel
.Pq override with Ev FRAMEWORK_TOUCH_MAP .
.It
Optionally runs the session user's chrome hook
.Pa ~/.framework_autorotate
when that file exists
.Pq override basename with Ev FRAMEWORK_AUTOROTATE_HOOK_NAME .
KDE, GNOME, and XFCE typically need no hook.
.It
On greeter recovery, may invoke
.Pa xlogin_recenter
.Pq override with Ev FRAMEWORK_AUTOROTATE_XLOGIN_RECENTER .
.El
.Pp
The session user for the chrome hook is chosen each rotate as follows:
the first non-root client on the X11 unix socket
.Pq any desktop or window manager ;
if none is found and an FVWM3 or BVWM FvwmMFL socket is present
.Pq e.g. Pa /tmp/fvwmmfl/fvwm_mfl_:0.sock for DISPLAY=:0 ,
the owner of that socket; otherwise
.Ev SUDO_USER
when running under
.Xr sudo 8
for foreground tests.
If no user is found, the chrome hook is skipped
.Pq display manager login screen, e.g. XDM, before a session exists .
.Sh RC.CONF
The package installs
.Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/framework_autorotate .
Typical settings:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
framework_autorotate_enable="YES"
framework_autorotate_mode="always"	# or "tablet"
framework_autorotate_display=":0"
framework_autorotate_hook=".framework_autorotate"
.Ed
.Pp
Logging is off by default.
Set
.Va framework_autorotate_logfile
to a path
.Pq e.g. Pa /var/log/framework_autorotate.log
to append daemon output there and enable verbose rotate messages.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ev DISPLAY
X11 display
.Pq default Cm :0 .
.It Ev XAUTHORITY
X authority file; the rc script selects an XDM cookie when present.
.It Ev FRAMEWORK_TOUCH_MAP
Path to the touch remap script
.Pq default Pa /usr/local/libexec/framework_autorotate/map-touchscreen .
.It Ev FRAMEWORK_AUTOROTATE_HOOK_NAME
Basename of the per-user chrome hook under
.Ev HOME
.Pq default Pa .framework_autorotate .
.It Ev FRAMEWORK_AUTOROTATE_XLOGIN_RECENTER
Path to
.Nm xlogin_recenter
.Pq default Pa /usr/local/libexec/framework_autorotate/xlogin_recenter .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /usr/local/sbin/framework_autorotate
Daemon binary.
.It Pa /usr/local/libexec/framework_autorotate/map-touchscreen
ILIT touch/stylus remap helper.
.It Pa /usr/local/libexec/framework_autorotate/xlogin_recenter
XDM greeter placement helper.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/framework_autorotate
Boot service.
.It Pa ~/.framework_autorotate
Optional per-user chrome hook.
.It Pa /var/run/framework_autorotate.pid
Supervisor pidfile.
.It Pa /var/log/framework_autorotate.log
Optional logfile when
.Va framework_autorotate_logfile
is set to this path
.Pq or another of your choosing .
.It Pa /dev/io
Required for EC access.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr florence 1 ,
.Xr xinput 1 ,
.Xr xrandr 1 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr daemon 8
